  "sources": {
    "L2-PDF1": {
      "format": "pdf",
      "page": 1,
      "path": "Notes/music/guitar project/PDF version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_2_Two_String_Transfer.pdf",
      "sha256": "cfcc4b3414400f5bfc2510c30c407f0d72e573ef8e899a184820202d67671ac8",
      "text": "108 Finger Permutations - Level 2\nTwo-String Transfer: 2+2 Adjacent-String Coordination\nThis level keeps the same 108 finger codes and fifth-position fret map, but moves every four-note cell across two strings.\n1. Same left-hand language\n1 = index / fret 5\n2 = middle / fret 6\n3 = ring / fret 7\n4 = pinky / fret 8\nNo position shift is added yet.\n2. New movement rule\nNotes 1-2: first string of the pair\nNotes 3-4: adjacent second string\nWalk E/A, A/D, D/G, G/B, B/e,\nthen return e/B through A/E.\n3. Practice one set at a time\nEach set contains 12 exercises.\nRun once starting with a downstroke.\nRun again starting with an upstroke.\nRotate your existing rhythm groupings.\nDo not run all 108 in one session.\nWorked example - code 1234\nThe digits stay in the order 1-2-3-4. Only the strings carrying them change.\nASCEND\ne|--------|--------|--------|--------|----7-8-|\nB|--------|--------|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|\nG|--------|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|\nD|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|--------|\nA|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|--------|--------|\nE|5-6-----|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nDESCEND\ne|5-6-----|--------|--------|--------|--------|\nB|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|--------|--------|\nG|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|--------|\nD|--------|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|--------|\nA|--------|--------|--------|----7-8-|5-6-----|\nE|--------|--------|--------|--------|----7-8-|\nProgression rule\n1\nChoose one 12-exercise set.\n2\nUse one rhythmic grouping for that session.\n3\nPlay every exercise up and down continuously.\n4\nRepeat with the opposite starting pick stroke.\n5\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next time.\n6\nAfter two errors or rising tension,\nreduce 4-6 BPM.\nAdvance when a full set is clean in both pick-start directions on two separate days.\nStandard tuning. Fifth position. Keep the code order intact on both ascent and descent.\nPage 1 of 10\n",
      "text_sha256": "2123bfb15b2aea242812cc9efece9799e42c7c49fc0a048bec2f05a5d405bf4e"
    },
    "L2-TXT1-12": {
      "first_line": 1,
      "format": "txt",
      "last_line": 12,
      "path": "Notes/music/guitar project/TXT version/108_Finger_Permutations_Level_2_Two_String_Transfer.txt",
      "sha256": "49ca027e8c7fee7b2c5437f93f8a5b5576e272e6cf888dbb1a82632749cec31a",
      "text": "108 FINGER PERMUTATIONS - LEVEL 2: TWO-STRING TRANSFER\nStandard tuning. Fifth position: 1=index/fret 5, 2=middle/fret 6, 3=ring/fret 7, 4=pinky/fret 8.\n\nMOVEMENT RULE\nFor every adjacent string pair, play digits 1-2 of the code on the first string and digits 3-4 on the second string.\nAscend through E/A, A/D, D/G, G/B, B/e. Descend through e/B, B/G, G/D, D/A, A/E.\nThe digit order never changes.\n\nPRACTICE RULE\nUse one 12-exercise set per session. Run each exercise once beginning with a downstroke and once beginning with an upstroke.\nRotate the existing straight-16th, triplet, and quintuplet groupings across sessions.\nAfter three clean loops, add 2 BPM next time. After two errors or rising tension, reduce 4-6 BPM.",
      "text_sha256": "21469f8bd5330c0263a7c9ebbf72f9b7ad5d96755f28c6db0c0eb2adcf97bdfa"
    },
    "L2-TXT15-15": {
